WEBVTT

NOTE Re-timed to Piper narration (en_US-ljspeech-high, LJ Speech (Keith Ito), public domain). Native review still required.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.987
Open Omni after installation. Read the welcome screens, choose your
controller glyphs, review privacy and select a universe. Move with the D-pad

2
00:00:09.987 --> 00:00:15.264
and select with A or Cross; B or Circle returns to the previous screen.

3
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:40.957
Choose a universe for its atmosphere; the underlying actions stay
consistent. Aurora, Cosmic, Arcade, Solstice, Metro, Sakura, Abyss, Prism,

4
00:00:40.957 --> 00:00:47.458
Atlas and Cassette are original styles. Reduced motion keeps transitions
still.

5
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:10.073
The console block prevents websites from reaching unapproved local services.
Verified app records define permitted pages. Ask maintainers to review a

6
00:01:10.073 --> 00:01:15.299
legitimate integration; do not disable protection to fix a blocked page.

7
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:39.210
Local discovery does not make browsing anonymous. Sites and download
services receive requests and apply their own privacy policies. Web pages

8
00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:48.104
must never receive Bloom Core’s token. History, links and passwords may be
stored locally; verify storage, encryption and deletion in the shipped

9
00:01:48.104 --> 00:01:49.072
build.

10
00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:09.813
Bloom Core runs in the background. If it is unavailable, apps should open
with their own defaults, but discovery and shared actions may be limited.

11
00:02:09.813 --> 00:02:14.974
Open the status page to see installed apps, versions and reported state.
